{# The search text, in the corpus's language. Retrieval only — the grader, the answer and
   the reply to the user all keep the user's own words.

   Every rule here exists because breaking it costs retrieval something specific:

   - a translated number, code or date is a term the index does not contain, and a fee
     row is found by "105,000 EGP" and nothing else;
   - localised digits (١٠٥٬٠٠٠) are a different token to BM25 than 105,000, so the one
     term that identifies the answer stops matching;
   - an answered or explained question adds terms the corpus never used, and every term
     absent from the target passage is dilution on both halves of the retrieval — the
     same argument `rag/graph_nodes.search_query` makes for cutting the child's name.

   The code does not trust this prompt: `query_translation._usable` rejects a reply that
   localises its digits, comes back in the wrong language, or runs several times longer
   than the question, and searches with the original instead. #}
Translate this school question into {{ language }}, as a parent would ask it.

Rules:
- Keep every number, currency amount, year-group code, date, email address and URL EXACTLY as written. "105,000 EGP" stays "105,000 EGP". "Year 3" stays "Year 3". "FS1" stays "FS1". "15/09" stays "15/09".
- Use Western digits (0-9) only. Never convert a number into any other numeral system.
- Translate the question and nothing else. Do not answer it, do not explain it, do not add background the user did not write.
- Keep it as short as the original.
- Reply with the translated question alone, with no quotes, no preamble and no notes.

